      "name": "ResetGlobalBufferState",
      "signature": "void ResetGlobalBufferState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Resets global buffer state by clearing flag and 4-byte section.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global state flag at 0x6ff39b5c is set (non-zero)\n2. If flag is set, call FOG.DLL ordinal 10043 with parameters (0x332, 0)\n3. Clear the global state flag by setting it to 0\n4. Clear 4 bytes in global string buffer at offsets 0x16c-0x16f\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  0x332 - Magic number passed to FOG.DLL function, likely error/event code\n  0x6ff39b5c - Global state flag location\n  0x16c-0x16f - Buffer offset range being cleared (4 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\n  No error checking performed - assumes FOG.DLL function always succeeds",
