      "name": "CopyPacketToGlobalBuffer",
      "signature": "void CopyPacketToGlobalBuffer(byte * pbSourceBuffer, uint dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Copy packet data to global buffer with memory allocation and network byte order conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Check if global buffer pointer is already allocated\n   - If allocated, call Ordinal_10043(0x37a, 0) to deallocate previous buffer\n2. Clear 4 bytes at global buffer offset 0x170-0x173 (reset header fields)\n3. Allocate new buffer using Ordinal_10042(899, 0) - allocates 899 bytes\n4. Store buffer size as first DWORD in allocated buffer\n5. Copy source data to allocated buffer using optimized memory copy:\n   - First loop: Copy in 4-byte chunks (dwBufferSize >> 2 iterations)\n   - Second loop: Copy remaining bytes (dwBufferSize & 3 iterations)\n6. Perform network byte order conversion for packets > 8 bytes and > 0x37 bytes:\n   - Read 16-bit value at offset 0x18 in allocated buffer\n   - Convert from network byte order using ntohs()\n   - Store converted value back as 32-bit value\n\nParameters:\n\npbSourceBuffer (byte *): Pointer to source packet data buffer\ndwBufferSize (uint): Size of source buffer in bytes\nIMPLICIT: Uses __fastcall convention (ECX=pbSourceBuffer, EDX=dwBufferSize)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Buffer size of exactly 8 bytes: Skips network byte order conversion\n- Buffer size <= 0x37 (55) bytes: Skips network byte order conversion  \n- Global buffer reuse: Deallocates existing buffer before allocating new one\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x37a (890): Deallocation identifier for Ordinal_10043\n899: Allocation size for Ordinal_10042 (packet buffer size)\n0x170-0x173: Global buffer header reset area (offsets 368-371)\n0x18 (24): Network field offset for byte order conversion\n0x37 (55): Minimum buffer size threshold for network conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
