      "name": "InitializeProcessInfo",
      "signature": "void InitializeProcessInfo(_PROCESS_INFORMATION * pProcessInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes a PROCESS_INFORMATION structure to zero values with SEH protection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up Structured Exception Handling (SEH) frame by saving current FS:[0x0] handler\n2. Push exception handler address (0x6fc31ec8) and sentinel value (-1) onto stack\n3. Load pProcessInfo parameter from stack at [ESP + 0x10]\n4. Clear ECX register using XOR ECX, ECX\n5. Update FS:[0x0] to point to new SEH frame on stack\n6. Zero out hProcess field at [EAX + 0x0]\n7. Zero out hThread field at [EAX + 0x4]\n8. Zero out dwProcessId field at [EAX + 0x8]\n9. Set exception handler sentinel to -1 at [ESP + 0x8]\n10. Zero out dwThreadId field at [EAX + 0xc]\n11. Restore exception code to -1 at [ESP + 0x8]\n12. Restore previous FS:[0x0] handler from stack\n13. Clean up 12 bytes from stack (3 SEH frame values) and return\n\nParameters:\npProcessInfo: Pointer to _PROCESS_INFORMATION structure (16 bytes total)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, structure initialized in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses SEH prologue/epilogue for exception safety\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention; RET 0x4 cleans parameter from stack\n- All four structure fields set to zero (NULL for handle fields, 0 for ID fields)\n- SEH frame constructed on stack with exception handler at 0x6fc31ec8\n\nStructure Layout (PROCESS_INFORMATION):\nOffset | Size | Field Name  | Type   | Description\n0x0    | 4    | hProcess    | HANDLE | Process handle (initialized to NULL)\n0x4    | 4    | hThread     | HANDLE | Thread handle (initialized to NULL)\n0x8    | 4    | dwProcessId | DWORD  | Process ID (initialized to 0)\n0xc    | 4    | dwThreadId  | DWORD  | Thread ID (initialized to 0)",
