      "name": "SetGameStateThreadSafe",
      "signature": "int SetGameStateThreadSafe(int newStateValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Sets a global game state value in a thread-safe manner using critical section synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section to acquire exclusive access to shared game state\n2. Load the newStateValue parameter from the stack\n3. Write newStateValue to the global game state variable at 0x6fc45830\n4. Leave critical section to release exclusive access\n5. Return success status (1) to caller\n\nParameters:\nnewStateValue (int): The state value to write to the global game state variable. This value is written atomically within the critical section to prevent race conditions.\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 to indicate successful assignment of the game state value. The return value is constant regardless of the input parameter value.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The critical section (0x6fc45a24) is a shared synchronization object used by 80+ functions throughout the binary to coordinate access to shared game state\n- The function always succeeds and always returns 1, with no error conditions or failure paths\n- Used in multi-threaded game engine to ensure thread-safe state modifications\n- The global game state variable (0x6fc45830) is accessed by 16+ functions for reading and writing game state",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:5d9568613687b1631f95f644a04443cd",
