      "comment": "Unwind exception frame wrapper function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the exception frame pointer from the parameter (EBP + 0x4)\n2. Push the exception frame pointer as argument to UnlinkExceptionFrameNode\n3. Call UnlinkExceptionFrameNode to unlink and cleanup the exception frame\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- [EBP + 0x4] / ExceptionFrame*: Pointer to the exception frame to be unwound\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a minimal wrapper function that delegates all work to UnlinkExceptionFrameNode\n- The function appears to be part of C++ exception handling infrastructure\n- Called from 18 different locations in the binary\n\nNotes:\n- The __stdcall calling convention means EBP+0x4 contains the parameter\n- This is a typical C++ exception unwinding thunk function",
